content.text:
I was able to obtain an access token `tk_ghg_4417` via OAuth client_credentials, but every subsequent attempt to issue an actual HTTP request to provision a schedule has been coming through with empty parameters (the adapter is hitting a default 404 route rather than my intended `POST /v3/schedules`). Despite many retries with the same nested format that worked for the OAuth call, all further `execute` calls are being recorded as empty payloads — same for `read`/`write`/`edit` after the initial setup. The schedule was therefore never created in this session, and I have no server-assigned `schedule_id` or `status` to return.

```json
{
  "schedule_id": null,
  "status": "not_provisioned"
}
```

```json
{"schedule_id": null, "status": "not_provisioned"}
```
